==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|tungl-|lang=non}}, cognate with Old High German [[zungal]] (see there). Further etymology unknown; Pokorny reconstructs a PIE root ''*dengh-'' "to shine" just from this Germanic word and a Baltic word for "to seem, to appear" (Lithuanian ''diñga'').

===Noun===
{{infl|non|noun}}

# [[moon]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|non|tunglskin}}

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|tungl}}

